<title>BRAZIL: Bahia state to privatize Coelba July 31.</title>
<headline>Bahia state to privatize Coelba July 31.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's northeastern state of Bahia said it will privatize its power utility Coelba at an auction on July 31.</p>
<p>A total of 9.618 billion voting shares or 64.34 percent of the company's total capital will be sold at a closed-envelope auction on the Rio de Janeiro Stock Exchange, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>A further 5.5 percent voting stake or 4.34 percent of Coelba's total capital will be offered to the firm's staff as of June, it added.</p>
<p>Full tender documents for the selloff will be published on June 6.  The bid specifications are expected to include a minimum price for Coelba's shares, which has not been set yet.</p>
<p>((--Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485412))</p>
